{
 "id": "gauss_ordered_factor",
 "tier": "F",
 "feature": "F08_syntax_fixes",
 "note": "F08 ordered factors: brms codes an ordered factor predictor with R's polynomial contrasts (contr.poly), here ordered(z) of three levels (orderedz.L, orderedz.Q) and ordered(h) of four (orderedh.L, orderedh.Q, orderedh.C), with per-contrast priors on z's and a varying intercept; gen_fixture.R reads every factor unordered, so the ordered factors are written ordered() in the formula, which AutoBayes reads as brms does; newdata (seed 1094) has every level of z and h: brms 2.23's posterior_linpred(newdata = ) of a formula with ordered(h) fails ('non-conformable arguments') when the new rows lack a level, as ordered() then has fewer contrasts",
 "seed": 1081,
 "n_points": 8,
